        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">Ad Martyras is a short letter of encouragement written by Tertullian around AD 197 to Christians imprisoned and awaiting execution. He urges them to see their prison as a training ground for the spirit and their coming death as a victory, not a defeat. The letter’s brevity and directness reveal Tertullian at his most pastoral, offering not theological argument but the companionship of a man who believed that the arena was the threshold of glory.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
